# Known Bug Patterns

See AGENTS/08-bug-patterns.md for full BAD/GOOD examples.

When reading or modifying any file, check for these patterns and fix them:

## Memory leaks
BAD:  `this.service.getData().subscribe(...)`
GOOD: `this.service.getData().pipe(takeUntilDestroyed()).subscribe(...)`

BAD:  `this.url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)` (never revoked)
GOOD: Push to `this.blobUrls[]`, revoke all in `ngOnDestroy`

## Auth failures
BAD:  `<img [src]="doc.contextParameters['thumbnail']?.url">`
GOOD: Fetch via `fetchThumbnail(uid)`, set signal with blob URL

BAD:  `fetch('/nuxeo/api/v1/id/' + uid)` (no auth header)
GOOD: `this.api.get('/nuxeo/api/v1/id/' + uid)` (interceptor adds auth)

## State bugs
BAD:  No state reset when route input changes
GOOD: `effect(() => { this.doc.set(null); this.loading.set(true); ... })`

BAD:  `error: () => { this.error.set('Failed'); }` (loading stays true)
GOOD: `error: () => { this.error.set('Failed'); this.loading.set(false); }`

## Reactive route state
BAD:  `signal(this.route.snapshot.queryParamMap.get('x') === '1')` for UI that should react to URL changes
GOOD: `toSignal(this.route.queryParamMap.pipe(map(qm => qm.get('x') === '1')), { requireSync: true })`
Why:  default router reuse keeps the same component instance when only query params change

## Opt-in feature capture
BAD:  Always populate `*ErrorDetail`/diagnostics signals on every failure
GOOD: Gate the capture behind the same flag that gates the rendering — `if (this.debugMode()) { ... }`
Why:  avoids retaining multi-MB JSON / HTML login bodies for users who never opted in

## Markdown
BAD:  `` `Application = Content Intelligence `` newline `` Connector` `` (code span split across newlines breaks rendering)
GOOD: Keep the whole backticked phrase on one line; wrap surrounding prose around it

## Security
BAD:  `nuxeoAuth: 'Administrator:Administrator'`
GOOD: `nuxeoAuth: process.env['NUXEO_AUTH'] ?? ''` + startup validation

## Architecture
BAD:  `import { X } from '@agentic-ui/feature-search'` (inside feature-browse)
GOOD: Move shared logic to `libs/shared/`, import from there

## Copilot will flag these — fix before creating the PR
